                            {provisionalArenaRows.map(item => <article class="excluded-result-card">
                                <div class="excluded-result-model"><span class="provisional-badge">PROVISIONAL</span><h3 title={item.name}>{item.name}</h3><span class="excluded-arena">Data Retrieval Bench</span></div>
                                <div class="excluded-result-score"><span>Provisional score</span><strong>{item.score.toFixed(1)}%</strong></div>
                                <div class="excluded-result-copy"><p>Not eligible for ranking because benchmark coverage is insufficient.</p><dl><div><dt>Active-level coverage</dt><dd>{item.canonical.coverage}</dd></div><div><dt>Operational result weight</dt><dd>{item.canonical.weightCoverage}</dd></div></dl></div>
                            </article>)}
                        </div>
                    </section>}
                </div>

                <div id="visual-benchmark-wrapper" class="hidden">
                    <header class="detail-hero">
                        <span class="detail-kicker">Arena 01 · Perception</span>
                        <h2>Visual Bench</h2>
                        <p>Five Active fixed-condition protocols for repeatable character localization and midpoint reasoning, with a sixth level Planned.</p>
                    </header>
                    <div class="benchmark-description">
                        <p>Visual Bench is the first benchmark in the Ultimate Bench series.<br>
                        It evaluates repeatable character recognition, localization, spatial binding, and midpoint reasoning by named chatbot product or interface configuration, including:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>recognizing characters</li>
                            <li>spatial understanding</li>
                            <li>consistency across generations</li>
                            <li>stability across different kinds of noise</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="methodology-link"><a href="/methodology/visual-bench/">View full Visual Bench methodology</a></p>
                        <p>The five Active levels use increasingly complex fixed task conditions. Each level repeats ten fixed questions across ten fresh, isolated conversations; its percentage is the number correct among 100 response instances, not 100 independent items. Level 6 remains Planned; its weight is reserved without a model result.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ranking-controls">
                        <label for="visual-ranking-method">Ranking Method:</label>
                        <select id="visual-ranking-method" class="ranking-select">
                            <option value="canonical">Progressive Level Weighting (official)</option>
                            <option value="baseline">Baseline Priority (exploratory)</option>
                            <option value="average">Flat Average (exploratory)</option>
                            <option value="crucible">Linear Level Multiplier (exploratory)</option>
                            <option value="resilience">Resilience Retention (exploratory)</option>
                        </select>
                        <small class="ranking-note">Alternate modes reorder this table only; canonical scores, Overall, and official ranks do not change.</small>
                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" id="visual-tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Visual ranking method explanation" aria-controls="visual-tooltip-text">ⓘ</button>
                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="visual-tooltip-text">Official Progressive Level Weighting order. Each Active level has twice the weight of the preceding level; alternate modes change ordering only.</div>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benchmark-desktop-container">
                        <div class="benchmark-container visual-table" id="visual-table-body">
                            <!-- Header Row -->
                            <div class="header-row unified-header-row">
                                <div class="col-header model-col-header" style="justify-content: flex-start; padding-left: 0.5rem;"><h3>MODEL</h3><div class="creature-icon"></div></div>
                                <div class="col-header mole-header">
                                    <div class="header-title-wrapper">
                                        <h3>MOLE</h3>
                                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Mole Level 1 explanation" aria-controls="tooltip-explanation-2">ⓘ</button>
                                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="tooltip-explanation-2"><strong>MOLE (Level 1):</strong> Ten fixed coordinate questions about an intact 10 × 10 character grid, repeated in ten fresh, isolated conversations. The result counts correct responses among 100 repeated response instances.</div>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="creature-icon mole-icon">
                                        <CreatureIcon creature="mole" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-header rhino-header">
                                    <div class="header-title-wrapper">
                                        <h3>RHINO</h3>
                                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Rhino Level 2 explanation" aria-controls="tooltip-explanation-3">ⓘ</button>
                                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="tooltip-explanation-3"><strong>RHINO (Level 2):</strong> The Mole grid loses the same lateral half of every column while retaining its logical grid and questions. Ten fixed questions are repeated in ten fresh, isolated conversations.</div>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="creature-icon rhino-icon">
                                        <CreatureIcon creature="rhino" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-header chimp-header">
                                    <div class="header-title-wrapper">
                                        <h3>CHIMPANZEE</h3>
                                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Chimpanzee Level 3 explanation" aria-controls="tooltip-explanation-4">ⓘ</button>
                                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="tooltip-explanation-4"><strong>CHIMPANZEE (Level 3):</strong> The Rhino image receives imperfect background removal, adding segmentation artifacts and information loss. The same ten questions are repeated in ten fresh, isolated conversations.</div>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="creature-icon chimp-icon">
                                        <CreatureIcon creature="chimpanzee" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-header owl-header">
                                    <div class="header-title-wrapper">
                                        <h3>OWL</h3>
                                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Owl Level 4 explanation" aria-controls="tooltip-explanation-5">ⓘ</button>
                                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="tooltip-explanation-5"><strong>OWL (Level 4):</strong> In a separate 17 × 11 grid with a central 5 × 3 spanning image, the model locates two named anchors and identifies their unique horizontal or vertical midpoint character. Ten fixed questions are repeated in ten fresh, isolated conversations.</div>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="creature-icon owl-icon">
                                        <CreatureIcon creature="owl" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-header eagle-header">
                                    <div class="header-title-wrapper">
                                        <h3>EAGLE</h3>
                                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Eagle Level 5 explanation" aria-controls="tooltip-explanation-6">ⓘ</button>
                                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="tooltip-explanation-6"><strong>EAGLE (Level 5):</strong> A larger, denser mixed-source grid combines animation, live action, irregular cropping, and selective color inversion. The model finds horizontal, vertical, or diagonal midpoint characters across ten fresh, isolated administrations.</div>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="creature-icon eagle-icon">
                                        <CreatureIcon creature="eagle" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-header beholder-header">
                                    <div class="header-title-wrapper">
                                        <h3>BEHOLDER</h3>
                                        <span class="tooltip-container">
                                            <button type="button" class="tooltip-icon" aria-label="Show Beholder Level 6 explanation" aria-controls="tooltip-explanation-7">ⓘ</button>
                                            <div class="tooltip-text" id="tooltip-explanation-7"><strong>BEHOLDER (Level 6):</strong> Planned evaluation. The Level 6 stimulus, task structure, scoring protocol, and measured capabilities have not yet been defined. No model results are currently available.</div>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="creature-icon beholder-icon">
                                        <CreatureIcon creature="beholder" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Rows Loop -->
                            {rows.map(i => {
                                const item = unifiedList[i];

                                return (
                                    <div class={`benchmark-row unified-row ${item.rank === null ? 'provisional-row' : ''}`} data-model-name={item.name} aria-label={`${item.name}, ${item.rank === null ? 'provisional, insufficient coverage for an official rank' : `official rank ${item.rank}`}`}>
                                        {/* Model Column */}
                                        <div class={`benchmark-cell model-cell ${getModelColorClass(item.name)}`}>
                                            <div class={`benchmark-content `}>
                                                <div class={`rank `} set:html={getRankDisplay(item.rank)}>
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="model-info" data-provider={getModelProvider(item.name).name}>
                                                    <div class="model-name-line">
                                                        <div class="model-name" data-release-date={item.releaseDate}>{item.name}</div>
                                                        {isNew(item.releaseDate) && <span class="new-badge">NEW</span>}{item.rank === null && <span class="provisional-badge">PROVISIONAL</span>}
                                                    </div>
                                                    {item.rank === null && <small class="coverage-note"><span>Insufficient coverage for an official rank</span><span>{item.coverage} · {item.weightCoverage}</span></small>}
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>

                                        {/* Challenge Columns */}
                                        <div class="benchmark-cell score-cell mole-score"><span class={` ${item.lvl1 === 0 || item.lvl1 === 'INVALID' ? 'zero-score-glow' : ''} ${item.lvl1 === bestAiScores.lvl1 && item.lvl1 > 0 ? 'best-score-glow' : ''}`}>{item.lvl1 !== undefined ? (typeof item.lvl1 === 'string' ? <span style="color: #9CA3AF; font-size: 0.75rem;">{item.lvl1}</span> : `${item.lvl1}%`) : ''}</span></div>
                                        <div class="benchmark-cell score-cell rhino-score"><span class={` ${item.lvl2 === 0 || item.lvl2 === 'INVALID' ? 'zero-score-glow' : ''} ${item.lvl2 === bestAiScores.lvl2 && item.lvl2 > 0 ? 'best-score-glow' : ''}`}>{item.lvl2 !== undefined ? (typeof item.lvl2 === 'string' ? <span style="color: #9CA3AF; font-size: 0.75rem;">{item.lvl2}</span> : `${item.lvl2}%`) : ''}</span></div>
                                        <div class="benchmark-cell score-cell chimp-score"><span class={` ${item.lvl3 === 0 || item.lvl3 === 'INVALID' ? 'zero-score-glow' : ''} ${item.lvl3 === bestAiScores.lvl3 && item.lvl3 > 0 ? 'best-score-glow' : ''}`}>{item.lvl3 !== undefined ? (typeof item.lvl3 === 'string' ? <span style="color: #9CA3AF; font-size: 0.75rem;">{item.lvl3}</span> : `${item.lvl3}%`) : ''}</span></div>
                                        <div class="benchmark-cell score-cell owl-score"><span class={` ${item.lvl4 === 0 || item.lvl4 === 'INVALID' ? 'zero-score-glow' : ''} ${item.lvl4 === bestAiScores.lvl4 && item.lvl4 > 0 ? 'best-score-glow' : ''}`}>{item.lvl4 !== undefined ? (typeof item.lvl4 === 'string' ? <span style="color: #9CA3AF; font-size: 0.75rem;">{item.lvl4}</span> : `${item.lvl4}%`) : ''}</span></div>
                                        <div class="benchmark-cell score-cell eagle-score"><span class={` ${item.lvl5 === 0 || item.lvl5 === 'INVALID' ? 'zero-score-glow' : ''} ${item.lvl5 === bestAiScores.lvl5 && item.lvl5 > 0 ? 'best-score-glow' : ''}`}>{item.lvl5 !== undefined ? (typeof item.lvl5 === 'string' ? <span style="color: #9CA3AF; font-size: 0.75rem;">{item.lvl5}</span> : `${item.lvl5}%`) : ''}</span></div>
                                        <div class="benchmark-cell score-cell beholder-score"><span class="status-badge planned" title="Planned future level. Protocol not yet defined.">Planned</span></div>
                                    </div>
                                );
                            })}



                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div id="chess-benchmark-wrapper" class="hidden">
                    <header class="detail-hero">
                        <span class="detail-kicker">Arena 03 · Strategy</span>
                        <h2>Chess Bench</h2>
                        <p>Five Active levels; Hydra is Locked and its weight 32 is reserved in the permanent denominator.</p>
                    </header>
                    <div class="benchmark-description">
                        <p>Chess Bench is the third benchmark in the Ultimate Bench series.<br>
                        Its goal is to measure how well AI models can play chess and solve complex positional puzzles. The challenges include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Understanding spatial coordinates and valid moves</li>
                            <li>Looking ahead multiple steps to predict opponent responses</li>
                            <li>Identifying forced mates and positional advantages</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>The levels are presented in increasingly difficult formats to test the limits of the AI models.</p>
